(3396314, 470332, 69776, '<td valign="top">wonderful shot, No faces but it doesnt need it to convay emotion in this one.</td>', 'wonderful shot, No faces but it doesnt need it to convay emotion in this one.', '2007-02-23 01:39:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396471, 471482, 26669, '<td valign="top">OK, back to the comments, first thing i notice, there is a lean towards the left, only .3deg or so but its there. You have just clipped the clock on the right also. for me there is too much empty space at the top of image and due to it being winter its too blank. <br/> <br/>i would have maybe titled the image "quarter past three"<br/>Good effort, keep trying</td>', 'OK, back to the comments, first thing i notice, there is a lean towards the left, only .3deg or so but its there. You have just clipped the clock on the right also. for me there is too much empty space at the top of image and due to it being winter its too blank.  i would have maybe titled the image "quarter past three"Good effort, keep trying', '2007-02-23 02:24:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396480, 471509, 26669, '<td valign="top">i like this shot, the title is also very good, i like the way the lights lead you away from the top center of the shot. the lone figure on the right with that shadow is also a nice touch. I myself would have gone for slightly more contrast but thats just me.<br/> <br/>"Bumping up one point"</td>', 'i like this shot, the title is also very good, i like the way the lights lead you away from the top center of the shot. the lone figure on the right with that shadow is also a nice touch. I myself would have gone for slightly more contrast but thats just me. "Bumping up one point"', '2007-02-23 02:26:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396486, 471095, 26669, '<td valign="top">i think the B&amp;W conversion could handle a little more contrast. i would have gone back and waited for a different time of day so the shadows on the right would be gone.  the title i would have played with and went with a little humor "Little Pixie" or something that refers to the pointed hood the person is wearing.  good effort</td>', 'i think the B&W conversion could handle a little more contrast. i would have gone back and waited for a different time of day so the shadows on the right would be gone.  the title i would have played with and went with a little humor "Little Pixie" or something that refers to the pointed hood the person is wearing.  good effort', '2007-02-23 02:28:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396497, 471014, 26669, '<td valign="top">i think this would have been a little better if you POV were different. Maybe going towards a lower POV. this may have brought a little more into the shot. As it is i think it is a little weak. there is too much emptyness in the top 3rd of the shop and it distracts me a little. i might have also played with the contrast and looked for a better tonal range.   good effort</td>', 'i think this would have been a little better if you POV were different. Maybe going towards a lower POV. this may have brought a little more into the shot. As it is i think it is a little weak. there is too much emptyness in the top 3rd of the shop and it distracts me a little. i might have also played with the contrast and looked for a better tonal range.   good effort', '2007-02-23 02:32:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396509, 470807, 26669, '<td valign="top">this shot i like, very good composition, great tonal range. and the look on the boys face is just great.  bumping up.</td>', 'this shot i like, very good composition, great tonal range. and the look on the boys face is just great.  bumping up.', '2007-02-23 02:34:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396519, 471485, 26669, '<td valign="top">the worst thing about this shot is the bottom right corner. that blur is bad and distracts far too much from the main subject. other than this i like the shot, theres lots going on, i want to see what was going on just out of shot to the left. good effort.</td>', 'the worst thing about this shot is the bottom right corner. that blur is bad and distracts far too much from the main subject. other than this i like the shot, theres lots going on, i want to see what was going on just out of shot to the left. good effort.', '2007-02-23 02:37:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396531, 471328, 26669, '<td valign="top">i don''t think this works to well, i don''t know if the car mirror was meant to add to this but IMO it does not. It also looks kind of an opportune shot that was taken as you drove by and thought " ahh quick camera lets take this"</td>', 'i don''t think this works to well, i don''t know if the car mirror was meant to add to this but IMO it does not. It also looks kind of an opportune shot that was taken as you drove by and thought " ahh quick camera lets take this"', '2007-02-23 02:40:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396532, 471446, 26669, '<td valign="top">i don''t know where the story is here, apart from it being an empty street. there is nothing to ponder over or think about. the empty street leads me into the black hole in mid right of the shot and i just stop. <br/> <br/>I also think the conversion does not work for you. its a little on the soft side of sepia.</td>', 'i don''t know where the story is here, apart from it being an empty street. there is nothing to ponder over or think about. the empty street leads me into the black hole in mid right of the shot and i just stop.  I also think the conversion does not work for you. its a little on the soft side of sepia.', '2007-02-23 02:40:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396535, 471484, 26669, '<td valign="top">after looking at this for a little longer on the 2nd passing i like it more. the POV low down looking back towards the person in the door way, i also like the owl overseeing proceedings,</td>', 'after looking at this for a little longer on the 2nd passing i like it more. the POV low down looking back towards the person in the door way, i also like the owl overseeing proceedings,', '2007-02-23 02:42:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396538, 471483, 68573, '<td valign="top">There is a lot to look into this image. Though a very simplistic composition, i felt like searching something here. Though you could have cloned out the crosswires at th centre</td>', 'There is a lot to look into this image. Though a very simplistic composition, i felt like searching something here. Though you could have cloned out the crosswires at th centre', '2007-02-23 02:43:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396541, 470922, 26669, '<td valign="top">ok i dont think this would be a street photo, even further a DNMC. this really looks like a family snap. the title is not conveyed enough as you can not make out the people around the little girl. there really is very little here for me thats states this is a "street photo"   sorry</td>', 'ok i dont think this would be a street photo, even further a DNMC. this really looks like a family snap. the title is not conveyed enough as you can not make out the people around the little girl. there really is very little here for me thats states this is a "street photo"   sorry', '2007-02-23 02:45:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396545, 470429, 68573, '<td valign="top">Nice image with so many attention points. I think you''ve done great justice to the theme</td>', 'Nice image with so many attention points. I think you''ve done great justice to the theme', '2007-02-23 02:47:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396547, 471350, 26669, '<td valign="top">For me Street Photography is more at home in an urban setting. rural settings don''t work. Although a nice shot i would have scored this better in a different challenge. <br/> <br/>Nice effort</td>', 'For me Street Photography is more at home in an urban setting. rural settings don''t work. Although a nice shot i would have scored this better in a different challenge.  Nice effort', '2007-02-23 02:47:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396549, 468872, 68573, '<td valign="top">Maybe a bigger crop could''ve given the feel of a street shot( though you have tried to convey it through snow) but i dont get that street feel in it</td>', 'Maybe a bigger crop could''ve given the feel of a street shot( though you have tried to convey it through snow) but i dont get that street feel in it', '2007-02-23 02:48:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396553, 469759, 26669, '<td valign="top">i like this shot a lot on my 2nd viewing. there is a clear divide here in the lamp-post and this also is in just the right place being push right of center. The street signs also giveing a Keep out vibe adds to the shot. <br/> <br/><b>Bumping up one point </b></td>', 'i like this shot a lot on my 2nd viewing. there is a clear divide here in the lamp-post and this also is in just the right place being push right of center. The street signs also giveing a Keep out vibe adds to the shot.  Bumping up one point ', '2007-02-23 02:49:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396554, 471308, 68573, '<td valign="top">nice capture and apt for this challenge. The back ground lights oin the left appear to be a little distracting and the focus is soft at places</td>', 'nice capture and apt for this challenge. The back ground lights oin the left appear to be a little distracting and the focus is soft at places', '2007-02-23 02:50:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396559, 469973, 26669, '<td valign="top">This is the second shot i have noticed that has been taking from a car as the person drives by. I think it may have been better if taken just after you passed the rickshaw to get the drivers facial expressions. also loose the door mirror. It adds nothing in appeal for the shot.</td>', 'This is the second shot i have noticed that has been taking from a car as the person drives by. I think it may have been better if taken just after you passed the rickshaw to get the drivers facial expressions. also loose the door mirror. It adds nothing in appeal for the shot.', '2007-02-23 02:51:21.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(3396562, 471505, 68573, '<td valign="top">nice composition though the tited horizon makes it look better and natural in this case</td>', 'nice composition though the tited horizon makes it look better and natural in this case', '2007-02-23 02:52:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396565, 471462, 26669, '<td valign="top">i must admit i am not a fan of colour street work. sometimes it works and other it falls flat in its face. This just about works as the colours are vibrant and punchy. the thing that spoils it for me is that the couple is a little too far back in the shot. and there is a little lean to the left.<br/> <br/>good effort</td>', 'i must admit i am not a fan of colour street work. sometimes it works and other it falls flat in its face. This just about works as the colours are vibrant and punchy. the thing that spoils it for me is that the couple is a little too far back in the shot. and there is a little lean to the left. good effort', '2007-02-23 02:54:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396569, 471498, 26669, '<td valign="top">this is a good shot for me. i think for the title i would have gone form , "Red Vs Blue". good idea to stick with colour.</td>', 'this is a good shot for me. i think for the title i would have gone form , "Red Vs Blue". good idea to stick with colour.', '2007-02-23 02:56:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396570, 471378, 68573, '<td valign="top">too many elements here and one has to look hard to dicover so many things . the carriage mixes up with the background to an extent that the top half is aalmost merging with the background. Maybe a a seletive desat or a color image would have been a better choice.</td>', 'too many elements here and one has to look hard to dicover so many things . the carriage mixes up with the background to an extent that the top half is aalmost merging with the background. Maybe a a seletive desat or a color image would have been a better choice.', '2007-02-23 02:56:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396573, 470719, 68573, '<td valign="top">nice colors of skay and this has a nice fresh feel to it. Great capture</td>', 'nice colors of skay and this has a nice fresh feel to it. Great capture', '2007-02-23 02:57:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396575, 469415, 68573, '<td valign="top">very beautiful. I like the leading lines in this composition as they take you right in</td>', 'very beautiful. I like the leading lines in this composition as they take you right in', '2007-02-23 02:58:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396577, 471520, 68573, '<td valign="top">a lot of symmetrical elements though i would have like a bit of more contrasts here</td>', 'a lot of symmetrical elements though i would have like a bit of more contrasts here', '2007-02-23 03:00:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396579, 471103, 26669, '<td valign="top">good shot, on 2nd viewing i like this a lot, The only thing i would have changed would be the contrast , really pushing the tonal range. I also like the reflection in the windows. The main subject also looking a little perplexed as to why you would be taking her photo.  <b>Bumping up a point</b></td>', 'good shot, on 2nd viewing i like this a lot, The only thing i would have changed would be the contrast , really pushing the tonal range. I also like the reflection in the windows. The main subject also looking a little perplexed as to why you would be taking her photo.  Bumping up a point', '2007-02-23 03:00:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396582, 470368, 68573, '<td valign="top">Lots of WOW factor in this. I love the lighting on the person sitting in the bench and the kind os surreal feel to it</td>', 'Lots of WOW factor in this. I love the lighting on the person sitting in the bench and the kind os surreal feel to it', '2007-02-23 03:02:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396584, 471233, 68573, '<td valign="top">Nice DOF but the focus is a bit soft</td>', 'Nice DOF but the focus is a bit soft', '2007-02-23 03:03:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396588, 470597, 26669, '<td valign="top">i like this, the title really made me look around the shot and that was great,  i have to say i am looking at this in work at about 8:00am, i am now hungry and want a Hot choc and Muffin.<br/> <br/><b>Bumping up a point</b></td>', 'i like this, the title really made me look around the shot and that was great,  i have to say i am looking at this in work at about 8:00am, i am now hungry and want a Hot choc and Muffin. Bumping up a point', '2007-02-23 03:04:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396590, 471048, 68573, '<td valign="top">A riot of colors here - lol. great expressions and a nice ''streety'' feel to it - a bit iffy on focus though</td>', 'A riot of colors here - lol. great expressions and a nice ''streety'' feel to it - a bit iffy on focus though', '2007-02-23 03:05:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396592, 471519, 68573, '<td valign="top">A nice capture with great warmth. Though it seems a little week on the theme ( no i am not a DMNC nazi!) great work</td>', 'A nice capture with great warmth. Though it seems a little week on the theme ( no i am not a DMNC nazi!) great work', '2007-02-23 03:06:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396594, 471344, 68573, '<td valign="top">Great capture - i like the colors and light on the right half</td>', 'Great capture - i like the colors and light on the right half', '2007-02-23 03:07:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396595, 467690, 68573, '<td valign="top">Wow - just love the sepia tones and the amazing clarity of the model. Great work</td>', 'Wow - just love the sepia tones and the amazing clarity of the model. Great work', '2007-02-23 03:09:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396596, 471480, 68573, '<td valign="top">nice capture. i like the shadows in the floor</td>', 'nice capture. i like the shadows in the floor', '2007-02-23 03:11:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396598, 470966, 68573, '<td valign="top">Amazing composition. Just love this. The warmth between the shild and the father adds a special charm to it. Certainly an image for the first page finish 9</td>', 'Amazing composition. Just love this. The warmth between the shild and the father adds a special charm to it. Certainly an image for the first page finish 9', '2007-02-23 03:14:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396603, 471128, 68573, '<td valign="top">Wow what a capture. Intriguing.... love the colors here and the unusual element in it</td>', 'Wow what a capture. Intriguing.... love the colors here and the unusual element in it', '2007-02-23 03:16:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396606, 470979, 68573, '<td valign="top">a nice old world feel to it and the coordinated expressions on the models adds such a wonderful twist to it</td>', 'a nice old world feel to it and the coordinated expressions on the models adds such a wonderful twist to it', '2007-02-23 03:18:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396612, 471521, 68573, '<td valign="top">nice use of advanced editing, the colors stand out wondefully</td>', 'nice use of advanced editing, the colors stand out wondefully', '2007-02-23 03:26:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396616, 471101, 68573, '<td valign="top">nice expressions, the man looks dejected but the dog is extremely camera concious. Great capture</td>', 'nice expressions, the man looks dejected but the dog is extremely camera concious. Great capture', '2007-02-23 03:28:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396708, 471078, 62812, '<td valign="top">Looks a bit too posed.<br/>Beautiful sky mind<br/>6</td>', 'Looks a bit too posed.Beautiful sky mind6', '2007-02-23 04:20:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396752, 471503, 36065, '<td valign="top">This is only the second image that I came across to vote on, but I bet that it will be one of my top few.  When it popped up, I almost immediately felt a sense of waiting.  I think that you could use a bit more contrast, perhaps a curves adjustment, but the composition is terrific.  The position of the girl draws the eye into the image to inspect all the interesting elements you included.  Nice toning, but I think I''d like to see the darks just a little darker.</td>', 'This is only the second image that I came across to vote on, but I bet that it will be one of my top few.  When it popped up, I almost immediately felt a sense of waiting.  I think that you could use a bit more contrast, perhaps a curves adjustment, but the composition is terrific.  The position of the girl draws the eye into the image to inspect all the interesting elements you included.  Nice toning, but I think I''d like to see the darks just a little darker.', '2007-02-23 05:31:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396753, 470317, 36065, '<td valign="top">Very nice motion pan and terrific tonal range.  I also like the strength of your composition in the capture.  About the only thing that I''d like to see changed would be the angle you took the shot.  I think if you were just a few inches higher (or taller), keeping the off of that horizontal line would have made this one even better.</td>', 'Very nice motion pan and terrific tonal range.  I also like the strength of your composition in the capture.  About the only thing that I''d like to see changed would be the angle you took the shot.  I think if you were just a few inches higher (or taller), keeping the off of that horizontal line would have made this one even better.', '2007-02-23 05:31:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396754, 471078, 36065, '<td valign="top">This capture has some terrific elements and the colors all pull each other together nicely.  I''d like to see more of her shadow, as it pulls strongly at the viewer''s eye to lead it right out of the frame, and I''d like to see a little bit of fill flash on her face to balance out the shadow/highlight that the sun created there.  I really, really like how the road pulls my eye deeeeeep into the image and leaves me looking to see what else is back there.</td>', 'This capture has some terrific elements and the colors all pull each other together nicely.  I''d like to see more of her shadow, as it pulls strongly at the viewer''s eye to lead it right out of the frame, and I''d like to see a little bit of fill flash on her face to balance out the shadow/highlight that the sun created there.  I really, really like how the road pulls my eye deeeeeep into the image and leaves me looking to see what else is back there.', '2007-02-23 05:31:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396755, 471332, 36065, '<td valign="top">Nice composition, nice toning and nice contrast.  I like how each element in this capture serves to pull my eye deeper into the image, but in varying directions.  Well seen and well executed.</td>', 'Nice composition, nice toning and nice contrast.  I like how each element in this capture serves to pull my eye deeper into the image, but in varying directions.  Well seen and well executed.', '2007-02-23 05:31:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396756, 471180, 36065, '<td valign="top">Excellent tonal range.  Your whites are well exposed without blowing detail, and your darks are very nice.  While I understand that there are limitations when shooting, I think shifting the frame a bit left would have made this one more appealing.  With this composition, your subjects are a bit too forced into the center.  Still, a very nice capture.</td>', 'Excellent tonal range.  Your whites are well exposed without blowing detail, and your darks are very nice.  While I understand that there are limitations when shooting, I think shifting the frame a bit left would have made this one more appealing.  With this composition, your subjects are a bit too forced into the center.  Still, a very nice capture.', '2007-02-23 05:31:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396757, 471290, 36065, '<td valign="top">I do get a broken feeling looking at this one.  I think you did a nice job meeting the spirit of the challenge, though some may bash you or provide stupid links regarding shooting homeless.  I like the composition, but I think it would be better zoomed out just a little bit.  I''d also like to see your toning with a bit more contrast.  As it is, the image looks just a little flat.</td>', 'I do get a broken feeling looking at this one.  I think you did a nice job meeting the spirit of the challenge, though some may bash you or provide stupid links regarding shooting homeless.  I like the composition, but I think it would be better zoomed out just a little bit.  I''d also like to see your toning with a bit more contrast.  As it is, the image looks just a little flat.', '2007-02-23 05:32:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396759, 467632, 36065, '<td valign="top">Its really hard to tell what is going on here.  While I really like strong contrast in most images, your darks are a little too dark, while your highlights are nicely lit.  This draws the eye to the lit areas of the image without pulling through the entire frame.  I also think that you are a bit too centered here.  While I am no stickler for the ''rules'' of photography, I think offsetting him a bit would have produced a much stronger composition.</td>', 'Its really hard to tell what is going on here.  While I really like strong contrast in most images, your darks are a little too dark, while your highlights are nicely lit.  This draws the eye to the lit areas of the image without pulling through the entire frame.  I also think that you are a bit too centered here.  While I am no stickler for the ''rules'' of photography, I think offsetting him a bit would have produced a much stronger composition.', '2007-02-23 05:32:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396760, 471286, 36065, '<td valign="top">I like the idea you started with here, but I think that your execution needed to be stronger.  I''d like to see the gentleman standing a bit more off the left border of the frame.  It feels cramped as is.  I''d also like to see a more contrasting tonal range.  With the harsh light here, the image looks a bit too flat.</td>', 'I like the idea you started with here, but I think that your execution needed to be stronger.  I''d like to see the gentleman standing a bit more off the left border of the frame.  It feels cramped as is.  I''d also like to see a more contrasting tonal range.  With the harsh light here, the image looks a bit too flat.', '2007-02-23 05:32:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396761, 471155, 36065, '<td valign="top">When I open this one up, my eye is immediately drawn to the bright sky deep into the image.  The problem is that there are no other elements that compete with that brightness to pull my eye away.  I like your toning, but the image is a bit too dark overall to keep the voter''s eye interested in the capture.</td>', 'When I open this one up, my eye is immediately drawn to the bright sky deep into the image.  The problem is that there are no other elements that compete with that brightness to pull my eye away.  I like your toning, but the image is a bit too dark overall to keep the voter''s eye interested in the capture.', '2007-02-23 05:32:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396762, 471097, 36065, '<td valign="top">You captured a great expression and a terrific feel of joy with this image.  It looks like the focus may be just a bit soft, and the background is a bit too busy.  Your depth of field was nicely used, but the distractions are still a bit too much back there.  Still, the expression makes the image.</td>', 'You captured a great expression and a terrific feel of joy with this image.  It looks like the focus may be just a bit soft, and the background is a bit too busy.  Your depth of field was nicely used, but the distractions are still a bit too much back there.  Still, the expression makes the image.', '2007-02-23 05:32:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396763, 470869, 36065, '<td valign="top">I really like you minimalistic-type of composition with this capture.  The textured wall makes for an interesting background that gives my eye plenty to roam around the frame inspecting.  I think that I''d like it better as a black and white.</td>', 'I really like you minimalistic-type of composition with this capture.  The textured wall makes for an interesting background that gives my eye plenty to roam around the frame inspecting.  I think that I''d like it better as a black and white.', '2007-02-23 05:32:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396764, 471167, 36065, '<td valign="top">You created a very interesting range of tones here.  It almost looks like selective desaturation with the grey of the building and the neutral coloring of the vehicles parked along the street.  I do feel that the large, colored flower pot is placed too much in the center of the image.  With its coloring and the lack of colors elsewhere, the eye is drawn and held there, not giving the voter ample opportunity to explore the image.  I think that you met the spirit of the challenge well, but the image could use a bit more interest.</td>', 'You created a very interesting range of tones here.  It almost looks like selective desaturation with the grey of the building and the neutral coloring of the vehicles parked along the street.  I do feel that the large, colored flower pot is placed too much in the center of the image.  With its coloring and the lack of colors elsewhere, the eye is drawn and held there, not giving the voter ample opportunity to explore the image.  I think that you met the spirit of the challenge well, but the image could use a bit more interest.', '2007-02-23 05:32:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396765, 468361, 36065, '<td valign="top">Interesting subject and great depth if field use.  I do feel a tilt to the image that seems more accidental rather than compositional.  I''d also like to see the monitor off the image border.  Overall, I like it.  I agree with your assessment mentioned in the comment you returned.  I do think that this one would make a nice wall-hanger.</td>', 'Interesting subject and great depth if field use.  I do feel a tilt to the image that seems more accidental rather than compositional.  I''d also like to see the monitor off the image border.  Overall, I like it.  I agree with your assessment mentioned in the comment you returned.  I do think that this one would make a nice wall-hanger.', '2007-02-23 05:33:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396766, 469207, 36065, '<td valign="top">Nice capture, but I think that you lost a good deal of interesting detail in the sky with you conversion to black and white.  I really like the scene here, but the shadow over the eyes of the subject is very distracting.  I like the feel of anger from both he and mother nature, but that shadow really hurt.</td>', 'Nice capture, but I think that you lost a good deal of interesting detail in the sky with you conversion to black and white.  I really like the scene here, but the shadow over the eyes of the subject is very distracting.  I like the feel of anger from both he and mother nature, but that shadow really hurt.', '2007-02-23 05:33:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396767, 471317, 36065, '<td valign="top">Great colors and very interesting shadows, but I think that filling the frame with the house makes this one feel too crowded.  Also, with the girl centered, I don''t fell that there is really anything to grab my eye and lead it around the frame.</td>', 'Great colors and very interesting shadows, but I think that filling the frame with the house makes this one feel too crowded.  Also, with the girl centered, I don''t fell that there is really anything to grab my eye and lead it around the frame.', '2007-02-23 05:33:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396768, 468786, 36065, '<td valign="top">I like the coloring here, but I''m not very fond of the composition.  If your point of view were higher, the perspective of the arch could have been better.  Or some perspective correction would have also made this one better.  Even still, I think it would have been more interesting with a tighter crop.</td>', 'I like the coloring here, but I''m not very fond of the composition.  If your point of view were higher, the perspective of the arch could have been better.  Or some perspective correction would have also made this one better.  Even still, I think it would have been more interesting with a tighter crop.', '2007-02-23 05:34:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396769, 470597, 36065, '<td valign="top">This one would have worked better in landscape orientation.  With his feet nearly touching the bottom of the frame and chopping off the price list, this one feels too tense.  I also tend to steer clear of art geared toward political statements.  Even still, you had a great start here.  With a simple flip of the camera, I think that this one would have been a great deal stronger.</td>', 'This one would have worked better in landscape orientation.  With his feet nearly touching the bottom of the frame and chopping off the price list, this one feels too tense.  I also tend to steer clear of art geared toward political statements.  Even still, you had a great start here.  With a simple flip of the camera, I think that this one would have been a great deal stronger.', '2007-02-23 05:34:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396770, 471259, 36065, '<td valign="top">Whoa!  That tree takes too much focus off your subject and he/she is a bit too centered.  I do like the angle of the ground paint.  It serves nicely to draw the viewer right into the main subject.  That is only after we get beyond that big tree in the foreground.  A different angle would have done wonders for this one.  Your lighting and tonal range are both pretty strong, so you had a nice scene that fit well into the challenge.</td>', 'Whoa!  That tree takes too much focus off your subject and he/she is a bit too centered.  I do like the angle of the ground paint.  It serves nicely to draw the viewer right into the main subject.  That is only after we get beyond that big tree in the foreground.  A different angle would have done wonders for this one.  Your lighting and tonal range are both pretty strong, so you had a nice scene that fit well into the challenge.', '2007-02-23 05:34:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396771, 471261, 36065, '<td valign="top">I like your selective focus here, but its one the wrong spot.  Either that or your shutter set too slow.  Your title suggest that the firefighter is the subject of the image, yet he is out of focus and too close to the edge of the frame.  It feels like he is about to walk right out of the image.  On the positive side of the image, your tonal range and coloring with this one is very, very nice.</td>', 'I like your selective focus here, but its one the wrong spot.  Either that or your shutter set too slow.  Your title suggest that the firefighter is the subject of the image, yet he is out of focus and too close to the edge of the frame.  It feels like he is about to walk right out of the image.  On the positive side of the image, your tonal range and coloring with this one is very, very nice.', '2007-02-23 05:34:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396773, 467728, 36065, '<td valign="top">I really like the scene you captured here, but I can''t see the snow.  I think that your use of selective coloring and desaturation sort of blended it all together.  I''d also like it better without the pickup truck in the background, or at least without the arse end chopped off.  I think that the selective coloring would have worked much better without it in the frame.  The red in the truck pulls the eye away from your subject.</td>', 'I really like the scene you captured here, but I can''t see the snow.  I think that your use of selective coloring and desaturation sort of blended it all together.  I''d also like it better without the pickup truck in the background, or at least without the arse end chopped off.  I think that the selective coloring would have worked much better without it in the frame.  The red in the truck pulls the eye away from your subject.', '2007-02-23 05:34:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396774, 470533, 36065, '<td valign="top">This is an interesting choice of subjects, but I feel that your execution is a bit lacking.  Composing this one with the child so close to the frame edge that he is facing gives a very uncomfortable, cramped feeling to the image.  You also lost a good deal of detail in his hair where your blow highlight is.  Softer light of a different time of day would have helped out a great deal.  I''m also not too wild about the green toning that you added.  With some work, this one could have been much better.</td>', 'This is an interesting choice of subjects, but I feel that your execution is a bit lacking.  Composing this one with the child so close to the frame edge that he is facing gives a very uncomfortable, cramped feeling to the image.  You also lost a good deal of detail in his hair where your blow highlight is.  Softer light of a different time of day would have helped out a great deal.  I''m also not too wild about the green toning that you added.  With some work, this one could have been much better.', '2007-02-23 05:34:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396775, 470834, 36065, '<td valign="top">Nice focus and nice work meeting the challenge, but this one is a bit too busy.  With all the business, there is no defined subject to grab the eye and pull it into the image.  It also feels cramped with the to individuals'' feet touching the bottom of the frame.</td>', 'Nice focus and nice work meeting the challenge, but this one is a bit too busy.  With all the business, there is no defined subject to grab the eye and pull it into the image.  It also feels cramped with the to individuals'' feet touching the bottom of the frame.', '2007-02-23 05:34:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396776, 470632, 36065, '<td valign="top">Too much dodging and burning.  The post-processing you chose alienates your subjects from the scene rather than making the viewer focus on them.  It looks like you had a nice scene that you started with, but the processing really hurt this one.</td>', 'Too much dodging and burning.  The post-processing you chose alienates your subjects from the scene rather than making the viewer focus on them.  It looks like you had a nice scene that you started with, but the processing really hurt this one.', '2007-02-23 05:34:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396777, 471240, 36065, '<td valign="top">I took a people photography class some years ago, and the first lesson was geared toward awkward places to chop the human body.  Cutting the body off at major joints almost always looks accidental rather than one''s compositional intent.  Chopping your subject off at the ankles makes this look more like a quick, shoot-from-the-hip snapshot than a composed image.  Always be aware of everything in your viewfinder, as well as its placement.</td>', 'I took a people photography class some years ago, and the first lesson was geared toward awkward places to chop the human body.  Cutting the body off at major joints almost always looks accidental rather than one''s compositional intent.  Chopping your subject off at the ankles makes this look more like a quick, shoot-from-the-hip snapshot than a composed image.  Always be aware of everything in your viewfinder, as well as its placement.', '2007-02-23 05:34:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396778, 471126, 36065, '<td valign="top">I took a people photography class some years ago, and the first lesson was geared toward awkward places to chop the human body.  Cutting the body off at major joints almost always looks accidental rather than one''s compositional intent.  Chopping these two at the knees makes this capture seem like more of a quick snapshot than a composed, thought-out image.</td>', 'I took a people photography class some years ago, and the first lesson was geared toward awkward places to chop the human body.  Cutting the body off at major joints almost always looks accidental rather than one''s compositional intent.  Chopping these two at the knees makes this capture seem like more of a quick snapshot than a composed, thought-out image.', '2007-02-23 05:34:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396779, 471276, 36065, '<td valign="top">I took a people photography class some years ago, and the first lesson was geared toward awkward places to chop the human body.  Cutting the body off at major joints almost always looks accidental rather than one''s compositional intent.  Chopping him off at the knees, as well as cramming them tightly into the frame makes this seem like more of a shot-from-the-hip snapshot than a thought-out, composed image.</td>', 'I took a people photography class some years ago, and the first lesson was geared toward awkward places to chop the human body.  Cutting the body off at major joints almost always looks accidental rather than one''s compositional intent.  Chopping him off at the knees, as well as cramming them tightly into the frame makes this seem like more of a shot-from-the-hip snapshot than a thought-out, composed image.', '2007-02-23 05:34:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396780, 469981, 36065, '<td valign="top">I took a people photography class some years ago, and the first lesson was geared toward awkward places to chop the human body.  Cutting the body off at major joints almost always looks accidental rather than one''s compositional intent.  You lost two at the waist and two at the knees (one walking and one sitting).  Then another is chopped at the ankles.  Always be aware of everything in your viewfinder and its placement.</td>', 'I took a people photography class some years ago, and the first lesson was geared toward awkward places to chop the human body.  Cutting the body off at major joints almost always looks accidental rather than one''s compositional intent.  You lost two at the waist and two at the knees (one walking and one sitting).  Then another is chopped at the ankles.  Always be aware of everything in your viewfinder and its placement.', '2007-02-23 05:35:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396781, 470842, 36065, '<td valign="top">While I am no stickler for the ''rules'' of photography, I do think that she is too centered.  I like your use of other elements in the image (people), as well as your depth of field to nicely frame and isolate her.  Your toning is fairly nice, but I think that the highlights could be a little hotter.  Overall, nice image that meets the challenge.</td>', 'While I am no stickler for the ''rules'' of photography, I do think that she is too centered.  I like your use of other elements in the image (people), as well as your depth of field to nicely frame and isolate her.  Your toning is fairly nice, but I think that the highlights could be a little hotter.  Overall, nice image that meets the challenge.', '2007-02-23 05:36:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396784, 471323, 36065, '<td valign="top">I like this one.  I think that the man could be a little more off the side of the frame, but it still sends a funny message.  I can just hear his mind thinking "what the hell" as he stands by the pile of snow advertising for car washes.  I''m not sure, though, if he''d rather be standing there or out washing cars.  I like the colors that you captured, giving this one an oddly warm feeling.  Nice eye and nice capture.</td>', 'I like this one.  I think that the man could be a little more off the side of the frame, but it still sends a funny message.  I can just hear his mind thinking "what the hell" as he stands by the pile of snow advertising for car washes.  I''m not sure, though, if he''d rather be standing there or out washing cars.  I like the colors that you captured, giving this one an oddly warm feeling.  Nice eye and nice capture.', '2007-02-23 05:42:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396787, 470584, 36065, '<td valign="top">Nice composition, though I''d like to see a little more space to the left of the frame.  With the bird facing that way, the crop is just a little too tight.  If the birds were looking toward the right, this one would have worked out just fine.  I like your use of vertical and horizontal lines in the frame to lead the viewer''s eye in and around.  It looks like you used a little too much dodging on his shadows, as I can see some pixelation and odd highlights.  Nice work meeting the challenge, and the title plays well with this one.  I like that you gave him a name, thus sharing a little more of his life with us.  This adds a great deal of interest and emotion to the image.  Strong work, just work on the post-processing a little more.</td>', 'Nice composition, though I''d like to see a little more space to the left of the frame.  With the bird facing that way, the crop is just a little too tight.  If the birds were looking toward the right, this one would have worked out just fine.  I like your use of vertical and horizontal lines in the frame to lead the viewer''s eye in and around.  It looks like you used a little too much dodging on his shadows, as I can see some pixelation and odd highlights.  Nice work meeting the challenge, and the title plays well with this one.  I like that you gave him a name, thus sharing a little more of his life with us.  This adds a great deal of interest and emotion to the image.  Strong work, just work on the post-processing a little more.', '2007-02-23 05:46:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396789, 468787, 36065, '<td valign="top">Your post-processing makes this one difficult to look at.  Everything ended up too soft, thus making it all look out of focus.  I think I''d rather see all the color in the frame, though your use of selective color is nicely done.  It looks natural outside the obvious lack of color in the background.  I do feel that you met the spirit of the challenge, but this one just doesn''t fit my taste in images.  I''d like to see a bit sharper focus.</td>', 'Your post-processing makes this one difficult to look at.  Everything ended up too soft, thus making it all look out of focus.  I think I''d rather see all the color in the frame, though your use of selective color is nicely done.  It looks natural outside the obvious lack of color in the background.  I do feel that you met the spirit of the challenge, but this one just doesn''t fit my taste in images.  I''d like to see a bit sharper focus.', '2007-02-23 05:48:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396791, 471346, 36065, '<td valign="top">Great color and I like the way the utility lines lead my eye into the image.  I can see where you were headed with this one, but I don''t really get the feeling that this one met the spirit if the challenge.  While I can clearly see that this is just off the street, and that I''d obviously see this scene while on the street, I think I''d like to see more of what is happening ON the street rather than just above it.  I also think that your crop is just a bit awkward.  Chopping off the buildings above the ground make this one seem more of an accidental snapshot rather than an intentionally composed image.  If you''d shifted the angle of the camera down a bit and included the bases of the buildings, I think that this one would have been a good deal stronger, even if the buildings and street remained in complete silhouette.</td>', 'Great color and I like the way the utility lines lead my eye into the image.  I can see where you were headed with this one, but I don''t really get the feeling that this one met the spirit if the challenge.  While I can clearly see that this is just off the street, and that I''d obviously see this scene while on the street, I think I''d like to see more of what is happening ON the street rather than just above it.  I also think that your crop is just a bit awkward.  Chopping off the buildings above the ground make this one seem more of an accidental snapshot rather than an intentionally composed image.  If you''d shifted the angle of the camera down a bit and included the bases of the buildings, I think that this one would have been a good deal stronger, even if the buildings and street remained in complete silhouette.', '2007-02-23 05:52:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396793, 470680, 36065, '<td valign="top">I love the performer and his instrument (didgeridoo?), but the composition needs work.  First off, while I am no stickler for the ''rules'' of photography, the performer is too centered inside the frame.  That causes the eye to see him and stop, almost as if it were boxed in.  Next, the lady on the phone, though nicely isolated with your depth of field, is very distracting.  Her white shirt competes far too strongly for attention with your subject.  Lastly, I''d like to see the end of the instrument.  Chopping it off right there leaves more of an accidental feel rather than an intentionally composed image.  I do like the strength in your toning.  You did a fine job not blowing the highlights, outside of the near-impossible white shirt, as well as maintaining nice detail in most of your shadows.  Great scene and fine work meeting the spirit of the challenge, but pay more attention to your composition.  Even a poorly exposed frame can be great with strong composition.</td>', 'I love the performer and his instrument (didgeridoo?), but the composition needs work.  First off, while I am no stickler for the ''rules'' of photography, the performer is too centered inside the frame.  That causes the eye to see him and stop, almost as if it were boxed in.  Next, the lady on the phone, though nicely isolated with your depth of field, is very distracting.  Her white shirt competes far too strongly for attention with your subject.  Lastly, I''d like to see the end of the instrument.  Chopping it off right there leaves more of an accidental feel rather than an intentionally composed image.  I do like the strength in your toning.  You did a fine job not blowing the highlights, outside of the near-impossible white shirt, as well as maintaining nice detail in most of your shadows.  Great scene and fine work meeting the spirit of the challenge, but pay more attention to your composition.  Even a poorly exposed frame can be great with strong composition.', '2007-02-23 05:57:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(3396798, 470986, 36065, '<td valign="top">Wow, what an odd trio.  No one there looks like they are remotely related to the others.  Nice eye and nice capture.  I think that the crop is just a bit too tight on the right hand lady''s head.  I''d like to see it loosened up just a little.  Also, I''d like to see your subjects more isolated from the background with a more shallow depth of field.  The headless individual behind the window is a bit distracting and competes a little for attention.  Pretty good toning, but your highlights look just a little too hot.</td>', 'Wow, what an odd trio.  No one there looks like they are remotely related to the others.  Nice eye and nice capture.  I think that the crop is just a bit too tight on the right hand lady''s head.  I''d like to see it loosened up just a little.  Also, I''d like to see your subjects more isolated from the background with a more shallow depth of field.  The headless individual behind the window is a bit distracting and competes a little for attention.  Pretty good toning, but your highlights look just a little too hot.', '2007-02-23 06:00:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(3397128, 471403, 68725, '<td valign="top">interesting...</td>', 'interesting...', '2007-02-23 08:59:20.000000', NULL, 1),
