(3407383, 470966, 20941, '<td valign="top">Fantastic shot, one of my ribbon picks</td>', 'Fantastic shot, one of my ribbon picks', '2007-02-26 17:35:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(3407403, 471505, 48890, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by SandyP:</b></div><hr/><i>Boooooooo to Agenkin!</i></td></tr></table> <br/>I re-read what I wrote, and I don''t see anything rude there. :)  You are free to boo me any time, though. :)<br/> <br/>To yanko - I still stand by my comment, to me this shot is really boring, something I''ve seen many times before, and without a twist.  But that''s just MHO.  I like one of your outtakes a bit more, though, it offers an unusual perspective:<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=473784" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/41337/thumb/473784.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/41337/thumb/473784.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/41337/thumb/473784.jpg"/></a></td>', 'Originally posted by SandyP:Boooooooo to Agenkin! I re-read what I wrote, and I don''t see anything rude there. :)  You are free to boo me any time, though. :) To yanko - I still stand by my comment, to me this shot is really boring, something I''ve seen many times before, and without a twist.  But that''s just MHO.  I like one of your outtakes a bit more, though, it offers an unusual perspective:', '2007-02-26 17:42:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(3407411, 471066, 20941, '<td valign="top">Great shot! Congrats on the Blue</td>', 'Great shot! Congrats on the Blue', '2007-02-26 17:48:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(3407412, 469974, 20941, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on a well deserved ribbon!! Fantastic work!</td>', 'Congratulations on a well deserved ribbon!! Fantastic work!', '2007-02-26 17:49:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(3407415, 470948, 62318, '<td valign="top">I''m not going to say too much about the photo, it is very well exposed and a creative shot. I''ll just say a few "nitpicks", very minor stuff and doesn''t take away from the shot. The bar going through the head of the other and the bar in line with the boot. It probably could have been recomposed to remove these little distractions. I also think it might be a little over sharpened for this resolution as I see some haloing and around the hat. <br/> <br/>Overall very minor stuff to a well composed, well thought out image. A good score and a very refreshing scene (the expression on the one makes the shot).</td>', 'I''m not going to say too much about the photo, it is very well exposed and a creative shot. I''ll just say a few "nitpicks", very minor stuff and doesn''t take away from the shot. The bar going through the head of the other and the bar in line with the boot. It probably could have been recomposed to remove these little distractions. I also think it might be a little over sharpened for this resolution as I see some haloing and around the hat.  Overall very minor stuff to a well composed, well thought out image. A good score and a very refreshing scene (the expression on the one makes the shot).', '2007-02-26 17:51:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(3407416, 469974, 48389, '<td valign="top">Congrats MAK, very nicly done!! :o)</td>', 'Congrats MAK, very nicly done!! :o)', '2007-02-26 17:52:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(3407422, 469974, 69537, '<td valign="top">Added to favorites. This is much better than the blue and the red, IMHO.</td>', 'Added to favorites. This is much better than the blue and the red, IMHO.', '2007-02-26 17:57:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(3407424, 470533, 62318, '<td valign="top">An interesting photo. It is one of those types of photos that I think would work best in a series rather than alone. It kind of grows on you the more you look at it. One think I might suggest it burning out the ear/face of the "other" child, since it does not add anything to the photo. While I don''t mind the "green" tinted one I do prefer the straight B&amp;W you have converted. <br/> <br/>A side note: I think P&amp;S cameras use a 4x3 or 5x7 format in general. I think the same photo with a typically 4x6 DSLR format might have even worked better, starting with the same point on the left. I would have loved to see a bit more of that handle bar. Nothing to do about that one, just a last minute notion.<br/> <br/>A terrific photo that I think was befitting of a higher rating in the challenge.</td>', 'An interesting photo. It is one of those types of photos that I think would work best in a series rather than alone. It kind of grows on you the more you look at it. One think I might suggest it burning out the ear/face of the "other" child, since it does not add anything to the photo. While I don''t mind the "green" tinted one I do prefer the straight B&W you have converted.  A side note: I think P&S cameras use a 4x3 or 5x7 format in general. I think the same photo with a typically 4x6 DSLR format might have even worked better, starting with the same point on the left. I would have loved to see a bit more of that handle bar. Nothing to do about that one, just a last minute notion. A terrific photo that I think was befitting of a higher rating in the challenge.', '2007-02-26 17:59:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(3407434, 471407, 62318, '<td valign="top">Slight crop off the right (to the door line), slight crop off left (remove headlight) and a bunch off the sky (back to 4x6 format) that is all I would change to this photo. A ton of character in this one. I love how everything is perfectly in focus except for UncleSam. Creative idea and superb title.</td>', 'Slight crop off the right (to the door line), slight crop off left (remove headlight) and a bunch off the sky (back to 4x6 format) that is all I would change to this photo. A ton of character in this one. I love how everything is perfectly in focus except for UncleSam. Creative idea and superb title.', '2007-02-26 18:06:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(3407440, 470533, 66384, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jaysonmc:</b></div><hr/><i> I think P&amp;S cameras use a 4x3 or 5x7 format in general.  I think the same photo with a typically 4x6 DSLR format might have even worked better. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Thanks for your comment Jason. I am going to see if there is a way I can change the aspect ratio of my shots to 4x6. I have been frustrated several times by the 4x3 format that I am currently using.</td>', 'Originally posted by jaysonmc: I think P&S cameras use a 4x3 or 5x7 format in general.  I think the same photo with a typically 4x6 DSLR format might have even worked better.  Thanks for your comment Jason. I am going to see if there is a way I can change the aspect ratio of my shots to 4x6. I have been frustrated several times by the 4x3 format that I am currently using.', '2007-02-26 18:08:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(3407473, 471160, 62318, '<td valign="top">Great score and a terrific placement. Funny I actually like "Your hair is fine" and "In Color" more though (a lot more). Being honest, I really wasn''t a fan of this picture. Don''t get me wrong, it is a good shot. I like the exposure, a good use of the frame, good depth and sharpness, and great textures. The expressions are wonderful and I like how the guy in the middle kind of stands out compared to dress and expression. I can see why this photo did so well for you. I think my problem is I "personally" can''t relate to the photo and really has nothing to do with the photo itself. Congrats again!</td>', 'Great score and a terrific placement. Funny I actually like "Your hair is fine" and "In Color" more though (a lot more). Being honest, I really wasn''t a fan of this picture. Don''t get me wrong, it is a good shot. I like the exposure, a good use of the frame, good depth and sharpness, and great textures. The expressions are wonderful and I like how the guy in the middle kind of stands out compared to dress and expression. I can see why this photo did so well for you. I think my problem is I "personally" can''t relate to the photo and really has nothing to do with the photo itself. Congrats again!', '2007-02-26 18:20:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(3407500, 469369, 62318, '<td valign="top">Great photo. I always believe that 90% of the time taking pictures of people''s backs is a bad thing. This picture falls under that other 10% as it gives good context to the photo. Sure, I think if you had another guy in the bench look back toward the lady, it would have been perfect, still it is terrific the way it is. The technicals are perfect: lighting, sharpness, focus, depth are all there. The composition is idea, nice low perspective catch the whole body of the subject, with the leading line in the bench pointing toward here. The texture of the ground and it''s wetness add a lot of character to the photo. A wonderful well executed shot. Congrats on the ribbon!</td>', 'Great photo. I always believe that 90% of the time taking pictures of people''s backs is a bad thing. This picture falls under that other 10% as it gives good context to the photo. Sure, I think if you had another guy in the bench look back toward the lady, it would have been perfect, still it is terrific the way it is. The technicals are perfect: lighting, sharpness, focus, depth are all there. The composition is idea, nice low perspective catch the whole body of the subject, with the leading line in the bench pointing toward here. The texture of the ground and it''s wetness add a lot of character to the photo. A wonderful well executed shot. Congrats on the ribbon!', '2007-02-26 18:30:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(3407510, 471073, 62318, '<td valign="top">I gave this a "6". I think the context is great, gives really expressive emotion to kinds and there fun. Wish I could have seen the other guys face fully, as his arm blocks distracts a bit. Maybe pull out a bit more. Still an interesting shot and a good photo of everyday life.</td>', 'I gave this a "6". I think the context is great, gives really expressive emotion to kinds and there fun. Wish I could have seen the other guys face fully, as his arm blocks distracts a bit. Maybe pull out a bit more. Still an interesting shot and a good photo of everyday life.', '2007-02-26 18:33:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(3407512, 469974, 7810, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the ribbon and your new PB. Your shot is stunning and was one of my favs for the challenge...Well done!</td>', 'Congrats on the ribbon and your new PB. Your shot is stunning and was one of my favs for the challenge...Well done!', '2007-02-26 18:34:31.000000', NULL, 0),
